Close the open items: cookies, notices, and honest branch reporting

Cookie contracts are now measured rather than guessed. ChatGPT's session
cookie is CHUNKED - the live jar carries __Secure-next-auth.session-token.0
and .1 and no unchunked name - so authCookiePattern is deliberately a
prefix match, and it stays a positive-only signal. Gemini's SID and
__Secure-1PSID/3PSID were re-verified. Names and lengths were read; values
never are.

Gemini's notice contract had never been calibrated because its wording has
never been seen: measured, a freshly loaded page has no overlay container
at all. Rather than invent a pattern - which would match nothing and report
"no notice" while a modal ate every click - dismissNotices now also accepts
STRUCTURAL specs that report any visible overlay and classify the text they
find, leaving anything unrecognised as kind 'unknown'. Because such a spec
matches any dialog, including one asking to delete a conversation, a button
is only ever clicked when its own label is in an anchored allowlist;
otherwise the only gesture is Escape, which cannot confirm anything.
Validated against a real Gemini page with two injected overlays: the
dismissible one classified rate_limit, the destructive one reported and its
"Excluir" button untouched.

Exports now carry branch: {index, total} per message and branch_pager /
branched_messages / branches_walked in the evidence, so a reader learns
whether sibling versions exist and whether they were visited.
branch_pager: false says the question was never asked, which is not the
same as "there are none". ChatGPT's pager could not be measured today - a
sibling needs a successful regeneration and the site declined one all
evening - and a guessed selector would look exactly like "no branches", so
PLAND records the exact calibration procedure instead.

Full acceptance recorded in PLAND 12.4: the OpenAI envelope, SSE
streaming, capabilities, threads, export over HTTP, typed errors, and the
whole CLI surface. A continuation costs 6.2s on the thread the tab already
holds and 35.5s when it must switch threads and rehydrate 44 messages.

90 unit tests.

